Important facts about the current implementation:

* HomeScreen currently contains a disabled Help & Credits button.
* That button currently points to the help screen.
* The standard fighter-select screen has a 48-slot roster, with available fighters as buttons and locked slots as non-interactive placeholders.
* Fighter #0001 is character ID "0001", is available, and occupies roster slot 0.
* Quick Battle’s Battle class currently always creates both P1 and a second fighter controlled by TrainingAIController.
* The normal HUD always creates P1, CPU, round/timer, and pause UI.
* Camera.follow(primary, secondary, dt) and Camera.snap(primary, secondary) already support a missing/null secondary fighter.
* MAPS directly drives the normal Quick Battle stage selector, so the Practice Ground map must not simply be added to MAPS.
* The repo already has reusable semi-transparent glass styling through .glass, .glass--panel, overlays, pause menus, etc.
* Keep Quick Battle behavior completely intact.

