js/stages/index.js

Visual direction

The stage should evoke the visual language of the classic Super Smash Bros. training stage, but it must be original Alva artwork implemented with Canvas rather than copied Nintendo assets.

Do not use Nintendo logos, textures, screenshots, ripped assets, or an exact traced layout.

The intended visual language is:

* clean training-room environment
* large geometric grid
* neutral white / pale-gray / cool-gray surfaces
* clearly visible darker grid lines
* occasional stronger major grid lines
* extremely minimal scenery
* no city/desert environmental clutter
* deliberately artificial “simulation room” feeling
* broad flat training floor
* crisp, readable geometry
* enough empty space for running, jumping, charging and testing attacks

Think of it as Alva’s own minimalist combat laboratory.

The grid should have visual depth without becoming distracting.

A possible treatment:

* pale gray background
* fine square grid across the backdrop
* stronger line every several cells
* subtle horizontal/vertical reference axes
* slightly darker playable floor
* simple edge treatment showing where the stage ends
* restrained shadows
* no particles or environmental hazards

The stage must remain visually compatible with Alva’s pixel-art fighter.

Keep it performant: generate/calculate static geometry once where possible rather than rebuilding expensive paths every frame.

There should be:

* no hazards
* no moving stage pieces
* no damaging environment
* no CPU-specific navigation requirements

Use a generous world size so the player can move around and experiment comfortably.

